From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ethan Hill <ethan.hill1999@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:19:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 13/21] KitKat UI P24: opaque shade panel + header carrier
 label polish

- donor 4.4 OPAQUE shade panel: flat #ff161616 surface
  (kitkat_shade_panel_bg) riding the panel expansion top-down in
  NotificationsQSContainerController, GONE outside the unlocked shade
- shade blur and zoom zeroed in the unlocked SHADE state
  (NotificationShadeDepthController)
- header band carries the opaque kitkat_shade_header_bg strip; donor
  ic_notify_button_bg pill retired from the clock
- CarrierTextManager pushes the cached carrier info (sLastInfo) on
  listen so the shade label renders instantly

los-24 port notes: CarrierTextManager gained satellite-mode plumbing
upstream (the cached push slots beside it); the shade carrier lives in
ShadeCarrierTextController. P18.5 scrim references are gone upstream.

Change-Id: Id2e3f405a6b7c8d9e0f1a2b3c4d5e6f708192031
